// aug13b round 2: a NATIVE interior recursive activation is the
// interp's transient fresh bind — it dispatches under a forced
// init view, so its consts fire per activation. The kernel
// threaded the PARENT's init flag instead, leaving every interior
// activation's const chain STALE on post-init cycles: the region
// emitted only in the becoming-selected cycle and went quiet
// forever after. The first is_self discriminator (the callee's
// sticky defined atomic) silently reverted on REBUILDS — the
// structural is_self match in CallSite::emit_clif is the correct
// key. interp [1:7 2:7] / pre-fix jit [1:7].
{let x = array::iter([i64:1, i64:2]); let rec f = |n: i64| -> i64 select n {i64:0 => i64:7, _ => i64:0 + f(n - i64:1)}; f(x)}